IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia-types`

-- Insurance Act 1966 — GOALS 6-7: THE POLICY AND THE POLICY OWNER
-- (First Schedule; ss 3(1), 66, 68, 146-152; nominations and payout, Part 3C
-- and s 150).
--
--   Goal 6: "Is this a Singapore policy, a life policy, a long-term accident
--   and health policy; is it valid; how much can be recovered; what may the
--   owner do after 3 years?"
--   Goal 7: "Is this nomination valid; who receives the death benefits; whom
--   may the insurer pay without probate, and how much?"
--
-- Source: ../source/IA1966.txt, ss 66-68, 131-136, 146-152 and the First
-- Schedule.

§ `Goals 6-7 — the policy`

§§ `Ordinary residence (First Schedule para 2(4)(a), (e))`

-- "(i) is a citizen of Singapore, unless he or she has resided outside
-- Singapore continuously for 5 or more years preceding the proposal date ...
-- and is not currently residing in Singapore; (ii) is a permanent resident,
-- unless he or she has resided in Singapore for less than a total of 183 days
-- in the 12 months preceding the proposal date ...; (iii) has a work pass or
-- permit ..., unless [the same]; or (iv) has a pass or permit ... that has a
-- duration longer than 90 days and has resided in Singapore continuously for
-- at least 90 days in the 12 months preceding". (e): part of a day counts.
@ref First Schedule para 2(4)(a), (e)
GIVEN r IS A `Residence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ordinarily resident in Singapore` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `status`
    WHEN `a citizen` THEN
        NOT (r's `years resided continuously outside Singapore before the proposal` AT LEAST 5 AND (NOT r's `currently residing in Singapore`))
    WHEN `a permanent resident`          THEN r's `days resided in Singapore in the 12 months before the proposal` AT LEAST 183
    WHEN `a work pass or permit holder`  THEN r's `days resided in Singapore in the 12 months before the proposal` AT LEAST 183
    WHEN `a holder of another pass longer than 90 days` THEN r's `days continuously resided in Singapore in those 12 months` AT LEAST 90
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE

§§ `Singapore policy or offshore policy (First Schedule para 2)`

-- para 2(1): issued in the course of the insurer's business in Singapore and
-- "(a) in relation to a life policy or accident and health policy ... (i)
-- where the policy owner is an individual, the policy owner or insured is
-- ordinarily resident in Singapore at the [proposal date]; (ii) where the
-- policy owner is not an individual — (A) the policy owner's address is or was
-- an address in Singapore ... or (B) ... covers an insured who is ordinarily
-- resident ...; (b) in relation to direct general insurance ..., a policy
-- where the risk arises in Singapore or — (i) where the insured is an
-- individual, the insured is ordinarily resident ...; or (ii) where the
-- insured is not an individual, the insured is a person resident in Singapore
-- or has a permanent establishment in Singapore". (2): not cargo carried from
-- outside Singapore to outside Singapore. (3): "Offshore policy" is any other
-- policy issued in the course of business in Singapore. (Treaty reinsurance,
-- (1)(c)-(d), turns on a 25% share of premiums; see `a Singapore treaty`.)
@ref First Schedule para 2(1)-(3)
GIVEN p IS A `Policy case`
GIVETH A STRING
`the policy is` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT p's `issued in the course of business in Singapore` THEN "neither: not issued in the course of business in Singapore"
           IF `Singapore`                                          THEN "a Singapore policy"
           OTHERWISE                                                    "an offshore policy"
    WHERE
        `resident` MEANS
            IF p's `the owner (or insured) is an individual`
            THEN `ordinarily resident in Singapore` (p's `residence of the owner or insured`)
            ELSE p's `a non-individual: Singapore address, residence or permanent establishment`
        `Singapore` MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `kind`
            WHEN `a general insurance policy` THEN
                (p's `the risk arises in Singapore` OR `resident`) AND (NOT p's `cargo carried between places outside Singapore`)
            OTHERWISE `resident`

-- para 2(1)(c)-(d): a treaty reinsurance is a Singapore policy where "more
-- than 25% of the total risks in terms of gross premiums arise in Singapore".
@ref First Schedule para 2(1)(c)-(d)
GIVEN `Singapore premiums` IS A NUMBER, `total premiums` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Singapore treaty, Singapore premiums` `Singapore premiums` `, of` `total premiums` IF
    `Singapore premiums` GREATER THAN `total premiums` TIMES 0.25

§§ `Classes (s 3(1); First Schedule paras 9, 10, 13)`

-- para 9(1): "long-term accident and health policy" — "(a) may ... be in force
-- for more than 5 years if it is not terminated earlier by the policy owner;
-- and (b) does not contain any term ... which permits the insurer to terminate
-- the policy unilaterally, other than ... on the ground of fraud or material
-- non-disclosure". para 10: any other is short-term.
-- s 3(1)(a): life business is life policies and long-term accident and health
-- policies; (b) general business is everything else.
@ref s 3(1); First Schedule paras 9, 10, 13
GIVEN p IS A `Policy case`
GIVETH A `Class of business`
`the class of business of` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `kind`
    WHEN `a life policy` THEN `life business`
    WHEN `an accident and health policy` THEN
        IF p's `may be in force more than 5 years, insurer cannot end it but for fraud or non-disclosure`
        THEN `life business` ELSE `general business`
    WHEN `a general insurance policy` THEN `general business`

§§ `Validity and what may be recovered (ss 146, 147, 151)`

-- s 146(1): a life policy issued by a licensed insurer "is void unless — (a)
-- the person effecting the insurance has an insurable interest ...; (b) the
-- life which is insured is that of — (i) the person effecting the insurance;
-- (ii) his or her spouse ...; (iii) his or her child or ward under the age of
-- 18 years ...; or (iv) any other person on whom the person effecting the
-- insurance is ... wholly or partly dependant; or (c) [a trust policy under
-- (3) or (4)]". (8): (1)(a), (b) do not affect policies issued before 1 January
-- 1967; (9): (1)(c) not those before 1 March 2009.
-- s 151(1): any other insurance "on any event wherein the person ... has no
-- interest" is void; (4): not insurance on ships or goods, or contracts of
-- indemnity.
@ref ss 146(1), (3)-(5), (8)-(9); 151(1), (4)
GIVEN p IS A `Policy case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy is valid for insurable interest` p IF
    CONSIDER p's `kind`
    WHEN `a life policy` THEN
            p's `issued on` LESS THAN YMD 1967 1 1
        OR  p's `insurable interest of the person effecting it` GREATER THAN 0
        OR  NOT p's `life insured` EQUALS `another person`
        OR  (p's `a trust policy meeting s 146(3) or (4)` AND p's `issued on` AT LEAST YMD 2009 3 1)
    OTHERWISE
            p's `insurance on ships or goods, or a contract of indemnity`
        OR  p's `insurable interest of the person effecting it` GREATER THAN 0

-- s 146(2): "Where subsection (1)(a) applies, the policy moneys payable ...
-- must not exceed the amount of the insurable interest at the time the
-- insurance is effected." s 151(3): "no greater sum may be recovered ... than
-- the amount or value of the interest". FORK F5: the s 146(2) cap applies only
-- where the policy stands on (1)(a) alone, not where (1)(b) or (c) also saves it.
@ref ss 146(2), 151(3)-(4)
GIVEN p IS A `Policy case`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most that may be recovered under` p MEANS
    IF NOT `the policy is valid for insurable interest` p THEN JUST 0
    ELSE CONSIDER p's `kind`
         WHEN `a life policy` THEN
             IF   p's `life insured` EQUALS `another person` AND (NOT p's `a trust policy meeting s 146(3) or (4)`) AND p's `issued on` AT LEAST YMD 1967 1 1
             THEN JUST (`the lesser of` (p's `sum insured`) (p's `insurable interest of the person effecting it`))
             ELSE JUST (p's `sum insured`)
         OTHERWISE
             IF   p's `insurance on ships or goods, or a contract of indemnity`
             THEN JUST (p's `sum insured`)
             ELSE JUST (`the lesser of` (p's `sum insured`) (p's `insurable interest of the person effecting it`))

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 147(1): "a person over the age of 10 years does not, by reason only of his
-- or her age, lack the capacity to enter into a contract of insurance; but a
-- person under the age of 16 years does not have the capacity ... except with
-- the written consent of his or her parent or guardian".
@ref s 147(1)
-- For a person of 10 or under the section says nothing, and the general law
-- of capacity (outside the source) decides: the encoding refuses (fork F8,
-- revised after the independent pass).
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has capacity to insure, aged` age `, with a parent's written consent:` consent IF
    IF age AT MOST 10
    THEN REFUSE "s 147 speaks only of persons over 10; capacity at 10 or under is for the general law"
    ELSE age AT LEAST 16 OR consent

§§ `The owner's rights in a life policy (ss 148, 149)`

-- s 149(1)-(3): "Where a life policy has been in force for 3 years or more" the
-- owner may surrender it for its surrender value; it "does not lapse and must
-- not be forfeited by reason of the non-payment of premiums"; and the owner may
-- "exchange the policy for a paid-up policy". (5): not for an annuity, nor a
-- policy under which no policy moneys are necessarily payable.
-- s 148(1): policy and surrender moneys are paid "without any deduction for
-- sums not due under the policy or under an agreement charging them on the
-- policy, unless the deduction is made with the consent of the person
-- entitled".
@ref ss 148(1)-(3), 149(1)-(5)
GIVEN p IS A `Policy case`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the owner's statutory rights under` p MEANS
    IF NOT p's `kind` EQUALS `a life policy` THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF p's `years in force` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT p's `an annuity, or no policy moneys necessarily payable`)
         THEN LIST "surrender for the surrender value (s 149(1))"
                   "no lapse or forfeiture for unpaid premiums (s 149(2))"
                   "exchange for a non-participating paid-up policy (s 149(3))"
                   "payment without deduction for sums not due under the policy, absent consent (s 148)"
         ELSE LIST "payment without deduction for sums not due under the policy, absent consent (s 148)"

§§ `Payments through intermediaries (ss 66, 68)`

-- s 66(1)-(2): payment by the insured to the intermediary "is a discharge, as
-- between the insured and the insurer, of any liability of the insured ... to
-- the extent of the amount of the payment"; (3): payment by the insurer to the
-- intermediary "does not discharge any liability of the insurer to the
-- insured"; (4): agreements to the contrary are void. s 68(2): the same for
-- payment to a group policy owner.
@ref ss 66(1)-(4), 68(2)
GIVEN owed IS A NUMBER, `paid to the intermediary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the insured still owes the insurer, owed` owed `, paid to the intermediary` `paid to the intermediary` MEANS
    IF owed GREATER THAN `paid to the intermediary` THEN owed MINUS `paid to the intermediary` ELSE 0

@ref s 66(3)
GIVEN owed IS A NUMBER, `paid to the intermediary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the insurer still owes the insured, owed` owed `, paid to the intermediary` `paid to the intermediary` MEANS owed

§§ `Nominations (ss 131-133)`

-- s 132(2)-(3): a trust nomination by an owner "who has attained the age of
-- 18 years" of "his or her spouse, his or her children, his or her spouse and
-- children or any of them", expressing "his or her intention to create a
-- trust", and providing "for the disposition of all policy moneys".
-- s 133(2)-(3): a revocable nomination by an owner of 18 of "any person",
-- providing "for the disposition of all death benefits".
@ref ss 132(2)-(3), 133(2)-(3)
GIVEN e IS AN `Estate facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nomination is valid` e IF
        e's `owner's age at nomination` AT LEAST 18
    AND sum (map (GIVEN n YIELD n's `portion`) (e's `nominees`)) EQUALS 1
    AND CONSIDER e's `nomination`
        WHEN `no nomination` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a trust nomination under s 132` THEN
                e's `intends to create a trust`
            AND all (GIVEN n YIELD n's `the owner's spouse or child`) (e's `nominees`)
        WHEN `a revocable nomination under s 133` THEN TRUE

-- s 133(5): where a nominee dies before the owner — (a) no survivor: the
-- nomination is revoked; (b) one survivor: that nominee takes the deceased's
-- portion; (c) several: each survivor adds "A/B × C" (the formula is an
-- image in the PDF), "where A is that surviving nominee's original portion
-- ...; B is the aggregate of all the surviving nominees' original portions
-- ...; and C is the deceased nominee's portion".
@ref s 133(5)
GIVEN nominees IS A LIST OF `Nominee`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Nominee`
`the nominees after deaths before the owner` nominees MEANS
    map (GIVEN n YIELD `Nominee` OF (n's `name`), (n's `the owner's spouse or child`), (`A` n DIVIDED BY `B` TIMES `C` PLUS `A` n), TRUE) `survivors`
    WHERE
        `survivors` MEANS filter (GIVEN n YIELD n's `alive`) nominees
        `A` n MEANS n's `portion`
        `B` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN n YIELD n's `portion`) `survivors`)
        `C` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN n YIELD n's `portion`) (filter (GIVEN n YIELD NOT n's `alive`) nominees))

-- s 132(4), (6): trust moneys "do not form part of the estate of the policy
-- owner and are not subject to his or her debts" (save the premiums paid to
-- defraud creditors, (5)). s 133(7): a revocable nomination is deemed revoked
-- if the owner deals with the policy, makes a later will disposing of all the
-- death benefits with the policy's particulars, or a later nomination.
-- s 133(8)-(9): the death benefits go "(a) if the last nomination is not and
-- is not deemed to be revoked, ... in accordance with the last nomination;
-- (b) if [it] is or is deemed to be revoked, and the last will is not revoked,
-- ... in accordance with the last will; or (c) ... in accordance with the
-- Intestate Succession Act 1967".
@ref ss 132(4)-(6), 133(1), (4), (7)-(9)
GIVEN e IS AN `Estate facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the death benefits go` e MEANS
    BRANCH IF `standing` AND e's `nomination` EQUALS `a trust nomination under s 132`
              THEN "to the trustees, in trust for the nominees; outside the owner's estate and debts (s 132(4))"
           IF `standing` AND e's `nomination` EQUALS `a revocable nomination under s 133`
              THEN "to the nominees, according to the last nomination (s 133(8)(a), (9)(a))"
           IF e's `a will disposing of all death benefits, not revoked`
              THEN "according to the last will (s 133(8)(b))"
           OTHERWISE "according to the Intestate Succession Act 1967 (s 133(8)(c), (9)(b))"
    WHERE
        `standing` MEANS
                `the nomination is valid` e
            AND NOT e's `nomination revoked or deemed revoked`
            AND NOT (e's `nomination` EQUALS `a revocable nomination under s 133` AND e's `dealt with the policy, or a later will or nomination disposes of it`)

-- s 132(7): a trust nomination may be revoked only with the prior written
-- consent of — where a trustee other than the owner exists — that trustee
-- (any one), or (no nominee having died) each adult nominee and a parent or
-- guardian of each minor nominee; otherwise, (no nominee having died) each
-- adult nominee and a parent or guardian of each minor nominee. (10): a
-- revocation without them is void.
@ref s 132(7), (10)
GIVEN `a trustee other than the owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `the trustee consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `a nominee has died` IS A BOOLEAN, `every adult nominee and minor's guardian consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a trust nomination may be revoked, trustee other than owner:` `a trustee other than the owner` `, trustee consents:` `the trustee consents` `, a nominee died:` `a nominee has died` `, nominees consent:` `every adult nominee and minor's guardian consents` IF
    IF `a trustee other than the owner`
    THEN `the trustee consents` OR ((NOT `a nominee has died`) AND `every adult nominee and minor's guardian consents`)
    -- (b) asks for consents only "so long as no nominee has died before the
    -- revocation"; after a death it names none (the prescribed requirements
    -- of (c) still apply, and are the caller's). Revised after the
    -- independent pass.
    ELSE `a nominee has died` OR `every adult nominee and minor's guardian consents`

§§ `Payment without probate (s 150)`

-- s 150(2), (7)-(10): on the owner's death the insurer may pay, without probate
-- or letters of administration — with notice of a standing trust nomination,
-- the trustee (or the nominees); of a standing revocable nomination, the
-- nominees; of a will disposing of the death benefits, its executor; and
-- otherwise "any proper claimant", up to "the amount prescribed by the
-- Authority" in aggregate (an input). (11): several claims under (10) are each
-- paid "A/B × C" (an image in the PDF), "where A is the amount which would
-- have been payable in respect of that claim had it been paid in full; B is the
-- total amount ... of all such claims ...; and C is the amount prescribed".
@ref s 150(2), (7)-(10), (12)
GIVEN e IS AN `Estate facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the insurer may pay without probate` e MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT e's `the insurer has written notice of the nomination or will`
              THEN "any proper claimant (executor, widow or widower, parent, child, sibling, nephew or niece), up to the prescribed amount (s 150(10))"
           IF `standing` AND e's `nomination` EQUALS `a trust nomination under s 132`
              THEN "the trustee for the nominees, or each nominee (or a minor's parent or guardian), up to that nominee's portion (s 150(7))"
           IF `standing` AND e's `nomination` EQUALS `a revocable nomination under s 133`
              THEN "each nominee (or a minor's parent or guardian, or a nominee's personal representative), up to that nominee's portion (s 150(8))"
           IF e's `a will disposing of all death benefits, not revoked`
              THEN "an executor of the will, up to the death benefits (s 150(9))"
           OTHERWISE "any proper claimant, up to the prescribed amount (s 150(10))"
    WHERE
        `standing` MEANS
                `the nomination is valid` e
            AND NOT e's `nomination revoked or deemed revoked`
            AND NOT (e's `nomination` EQUALS `a revocable nomination under s 133` AND e's `dealt with the policy, or a later will or nomination disposes of it`)

@ref s 150(11)
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `B` IS A NUMBER, `C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a proper claimant's payment, claim in full` `A` `, all claims in full` `B` `, prescribed amount` `C` MEANS
    IF `B` AT MOST `C` THEN `A` ELSE `A` DIVIDED BY `B` TIMES `C`

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 132(1), (5), (8)-(9), (11)-(15), 133(4), (6), 134-136, 150(1), (3)-(6), (13)-(14), 152
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`policy provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 132(1): trust nominations do not apply to Dependants' Protection Insurance Scheme policies, CPF investment policies or prescribed policies"
         "s 132(5): premiums paid to defraud creditors are recoverable by the creditors out of the trust moneys"
         "s 132(9), (11): varying a trust-nominated policy needs the same consents as revocation; an insurer executing an instruction without them is liable to the nominees"
         "s 132(12)-(15): trustees of policy moneys (adults only) are appointed by the owner or the Court; the policy vests in them on notice to the insurer"
         "s 133(6): in a common accident, the younger is deemed to survive the elder"
         "ss 134, 135: insurers keep a register of nominees; co-operative society nominations"
         "s 150(1): living benefits under a trust nomination may be paid to the trustee or nominees"
         "s 150(3)-(6): payments before estate duty clearance, up to a prescribed amount, with notice to the Commissioner of Estate Duties"
         "s 152: no action lies for a fire that began accidentally, saving landlord and tenant agreements"
